WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.810
- The Supreme court
just heard oral argument

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.470
in an incredibly interesting
First Amendment case related

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.400
to students.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.233
You might not know this,

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:09.090
but students do have
First Amendment rights.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.760
After all public schools
are an arm of the government

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.730
so if they punish you for your speech,

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.090
even if you are a minor student,

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.770
then that might be a violation
of the First Amendment,

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.864
and this is an incredible
case where a student

00:00:20.864 --> 00:00:23.821
said some curse words on
social media, on Snapchat,

00:00:23.821 --> 00:00:27.627
and this was outside of school,
but someone brought that

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.170
into the school and then
the school punished her

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.100
for saying these curse words,
and so, the question is

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.040
where does the right of the students end?

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.229
Can they be punished in school

00:00:37.229 --> 00:00:39.700
for something they did outside of school?

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:40.533
It's going to be

00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:42.120
an incredibly interesting
First Amendment case

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.030
and we'll see where the lines are drawn

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.800
with respect to student rights,

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.753
and so we'll see you in court.

